{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.witness_fails_once_conjugate_present","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.witness_fails_once_conjugate_present","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L211-L218","doc":"The contrast that isolates the cause.  Keep the object and add its\nconjugate, and it fails.  So what the witness above relies on is not the\ndimension and not the multiplicity, but the **absence of the conjugate** — the\nfreedom a self-dual category does not have, since there the conjugate is always\npresent whenever the irrep is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.parity_invariant_fails_in_complex_sector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.parity_invariant_fails_in_complex_sector","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L204-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wComplexType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wComplexType","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L193-L202","doc":"**The scope statement.**  There is an object that passes the `Sym²` gate and\nhas **odd** dimension.  So `Sym2GateMultiplicity.even_dimOfMult_of_gate` — \"a\npassing object has even dimension\" — has no analogue once irreps are allowed to\nbe non-self-dual, and `dimOfMult_ne_three_of_gate` must be read as a theorem\nabout the self-dual sector, not as a bar on dimension `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.complex_three_passes_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.complex_three_passes_gate","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L187-L191","doc":"**The witness.**  It passes the gate: the only occurring irrep is `0`, whose\nconjugate `1` has multiplicity `0`, so no cross term survives — and `Sym²` of a\ncomplex-type irrep contains no singlet of its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.complex_three_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.complex_three_dim","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L184-L185","doc":"The object has dimension `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wDual_zero_ne_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wDual_zero_ne_self","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L180-L182","doc":"The conjugate is genuinely a **different** irrep — the complex-type\nhypothesis, stated rather than assumed silently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wDual_involutive_on_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wDual_involutive_on_pair","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L177-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wDual","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L173-L175","doc":"Conjugation: `0 ↔ 1`, a genuine involution with **no fixed point** among\nthe two indices — this is what `FS = 0`, complex type, means. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wDim","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L170-L171","doc":"Dimensions: irrep `0` (and its conjugate `1`) are three-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.wMult","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L167-L168","doc":"Multiplicity: one copy of irrep `0`, nothing else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.conjugate_pair_fails_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.conjugate_pair_fails_gate","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L151-L160","doc":"Within the complex sector, an irrep **and** its conjugate both present is\nexactly what fails the gate.  (Contrast the self-dual sector, where the\nrestrictive mechanism is instead the binomial self-pairing of\n`Sym2GateMultiplicity` — a different quantity, and one that lets a symplectic\nirrep through at multiplicity one.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.complexType_gate_iff_no_conjugate_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.complexType_gate_iff_no_conjugate_pair","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L132-L149","doc":"On the complex sector the gate has a **conjugate-avoidance** reading: it\npasses exactly when the object never contains an irrep together with its\nconjugate.\n\n**The hypothesis is not used in the proof, and that is the point.**  The\nequivalence is pure arithmetic — it holds for any `dual` whatever, which is why\nit is discharged by `crossSingletCount_eq_zero_iff` alone.  What `ComplexTypeOn`\nbuys is not the *equivalence* but the right to call the left-hand side a\n**singlet count**: off the complex sector `crossSingletCount` is not the singlet\ncount at all (see the scope paragraph on the definition), so the equivalence\nwould be a true statement about the wrong quantity.  Carrying the hypothesis\nforces call sites to declare the sector rather than inherit the reading\nsilently.  Named accordingly — the interpretation, not the arithmetic, is what\nis conditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.ComplexTypeOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.ComplexTypeOn","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L127-L130","doc":"**Complex type on `S`**: no occurring irrep is its own dual.  This is the\n`FS = 0` hypothesis, and it is what licenses reading `crossSingletCount` as the\nsinglet count at all — see the scope paragraph on the definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.crossSingletCount_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.crossSingletCount_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L119-L125","doc":"**The gate in the complex sector.**  The cross terms vanish exactly when no\nirrep occurs together with its conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.crossSingletCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.crossSingletCount","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L93-L115","doc":"The cross-term singlet count **on the complex sector**.  `V_i ⊗ V_j`\ncontains a singlet exactly when `V_j ≅ V_i^*`, so the `V_i` isotypic component\npairs against the `V_{dual i}` one to contribute `m_i · m_{dual i}`.\n\nSummed over `i ∈ S` this counts each conjugate pair from **both ends**, so it is\na count of *ordered* singlet-producing pairings — twice the unordered number.\nOnly its **vanishing** is used below, and that is unaffected; the factor is\nrecorded rather than quietly divided out.\n\n**Scope, and it is not cosmetic.**  This is the complete singlet count only when\nevery occurring irrep is of **complex type** (`ComplexTypeOn` below): then\n`Sym²(V_i)` carries no singlet of its own and the cross terms are all there is.\nOn a **self-dual** irrep it is simply the wrong quantity — the true contribution\nis `C(m+1, 2)` (orthogonal) or `C(m, 2)` (symplectic), per\n`Sym2GateMultiplicity.sym2SingletCount`, and the symplectic case differs from\n`m²` exactly where it matters: at `m = 1` the binomial vanishes and `m²` does\nnot.  Reading `m_i · m_{dual i}` as a singlet count at `dual i = i` would\ncontradict `Sym2GateMultiplicity.fundamental_passes_gate`, in which the\nself-dual 2-dimensional fibre is present and **passes**.  Hence the\n`ComplexTypeOn` hypothesis is carried explicitly wherever the count is read as\na gate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.dimOfMultGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateComplexType.dimOfMultGen","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateComplexType.lean#L90-L91","doc":"`dim W = Σ_i m_i · d_i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}